From 9c5199ee810b465495ca379d528740418cee4074 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TuNV <steven.nguyen.bn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 13:28:41 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] [icwmp P3b fix] wlansec_mtk.c: drop the static get_empty, the
 engine has one

  wlansec_mtk.c:400: error: static declaration of 'get_empty' follows
                     non-static declaration
  dmtr098.h:485: note: previous declaration of 'get_empty' was here

Same body (*value = ""), so the file now uses the engine's get_empty().
deviceinfo_mtk.c hit this exact clash earlier in the port (analysis 11.x);
it came back because nothing checked for it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 public/libs/libicwmp_dm/src/sdk/mtk/dm098/wlansec_mtk.c | 5 -----
 1 file changed, 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/public/libs/libicwmp_dm/src/sdk/mtk/dm098/wlansec_mtk.c b/public/libs/libicwmp_dm/src/sdk/mtk/dm098/wlansec_mtk.c
index 7305695..6e92ed8 100644
--- a/public/libs/libicwmp_dm/src/sdk/mtk/dm098/wlansec_mtk.c
+++ b/public/libs/libicwmp_dm/src/sdk/mtk/dm098/wlansec_mtk.c
@@ -397,11 +397,6 @@ static int set_wep_key_index(char *refparam, struct dmctx *ctx, void *data, char
 	return 0;
 }
 
-static int get_empty(char *refparam, struct dmctx *ctx, void *data, char *instance, char **value)
-{
-	*value = "";
-	return 0;
-}
 
 /* key1..key4, length decided by the WEP level: 5 or 10 for 40 bit, 13 or 26
  * for 104 bit, the longer form being hex */
-- 
2.34.1

